f 17592186045417] [17592186119986 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119986 #edb/ref 1045 "Volumes of Rectangular Solids" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119986 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119986 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119986 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119986 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "eed5aa9e-ed1f-5edb-990e-f8643f3d4226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-10228" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120060 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120060 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/17/175d15b140a660148d8890cf32f4c4b79a43ff86d82c7e4461174326dfa9eeca.png)\n\nFind the volume of the rectangular prism shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "354c9af3-a204-5b30-bbc0-46ae605292f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120060 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=7\\,\\text{in},\\,w=2\\,\\text{in},\\,h=3\\,\\text{in}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=7\\cdot 2\\cdot 3=42\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186116734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1071 "A bar of chocolate in the form of a rectangular prism is $9\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $2\\,\\text{cm}$ high. If the chocolate costs $$0.02$ per cubic centimeter, what is the value of four identical bars of chocolate?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9fb6d92-70dd-5c7f-9979-070fe590bd5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120088 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the volume of the bar of chocolate.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9,\\,w=5,\\,h=2\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=9\\cdot 5\\cdot 2=90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe total volume of the four bars of chocolate is\n\n$$\n90\\cdot 4=360\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the cost of four chocolate bars is\n\n$$\n360\\cdot 0.02=$7.20.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120174 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120174 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32206" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120174 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120174 #edb/ref 1071 "The height of a rectangular solid is $15\\,\\text{cm}$ and its volume is $675\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$ If the base of the solid is a square, find the length of the solid." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120174 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4974d95-bce3-5ff7-8461-630c37925bee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120174 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSince the base of the rectangular solid is a square, we have that \n\n$$\nl=w.\n$$\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nV=675,\\,h=15,\\,w=l\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =lwh \\\\ V & ={l}^{2}h \\\\ 675 & ={l}^{2}\\cdot 15 \\\\ {l}^{2} & =45 \\\\ l & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length is $3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120806 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120806 #edb/ref 1061 33545 #edb/re